{"toolCallId":"call_f3c647afadbf4b16940561a2531fb558","status":"completed","content":[{"type":"content","content":{"type":"text","text":"\n---\n\n## 6. LEVEL RECOMMENDATION\n\n### recommend-level.sh\n\nRecommends appropriate documentation level based on feature characteristics.\n\n**Usage:**\n```bash\n# Basic recommendation\nbash .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/recommend-level.sh \"Add user authentication\"\n\n# With feature flags\nbash .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/recommend-level.sh --auth --api \"Add OAuth login\"\n```\n\n**Feature Flags:**\n| Flag | Effect |\n|------|--------|\n=== quick-ref 50-62 ===\n|-----------|-------|-------------------|-------------------|\n| Any task (baseline) | 1 | spec.md + plan.md + tasks.md + implementation-summary.md | resource-map.md (any level) |\n| Needs QA validation | 2 | L1 + acceptance-criteria.md | resource-map.md (any level) |\n| Complex/architectural | 3 | L2 + decision-record.md | research/research.md, resource-map.md |\n| Enterprise/governance heavy | 3+ | L3 file set rendered at Level 3+ | research/research.md, resource-map.md |\n\n**LOC as one input to `runtime/cli/spec/recommend-level.sh`, which scores it with file count and risk:**\n- <100 LOC suggests Level 1\n- 100-499 LOC suggests Level 2\n- >=500 LOC suggests Level 3\n- High complexity/risk and governance needs suggest Level 3+\n\n---\n=== quick-ref 570-582 ===\n- **ALWAYS get user approval** - Explicit \"yes\" before file changes\n- **Use distributed governance for spec docs** — Any agent writing packet markdown must use the level templates, run `validate.sh --strict`, and route continuity refreshes through `/speckit:save`. Preserve `@deep-research` ownership of `research/research.md` and `@debug` ownership of `debug-delegation.md`.\n\n### Enforcement\n\n- **Verify required templates exist** before claiming completion\n- **LOC is one scored input** - run `recommend-level.sh` and go higher when your judgment disagrees\n- **Enforcement is `validate.sh --strict` plus `check-completion.sh`** - run both before claiming done\n\n### Applies to ALL\n\n- Code files (*.js, *.ts, *.py, *.css, *.html)\n- Documentation files (*.md, README, docs/)\n"}}],"_meta":{"cognition.ai/cwd":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Code-Environment-Public/fcd93cd7-b3f2-45e6-b976-87fabe792df3/scratchpad/speed-loop/w4fbf614733/tree","terminal_exit":{"terminal_id":"baa774","exit_code":0,"signal":null},"cognition.ai/inferenceToolName":"exec"}}
{"toolCallId":"call_fae3db5365c648b8a8b7164a512a25eb","status":"completed","content":[{"type":"content","content":{"type":"text","text":"{\n  \"clean\": \"node -e \\\"require('node:fs').rmSync('dist', { recursive: true, force: true })\\\"\",\n  \"prepare-build\": \"node lib/dist-freshness.cjs prepare-build --package system-spec-kit/runtime/cli --entry default && node lib/dist-freshness.cjs prepare-build --package system-spec-kit/runtime/cli --entry is-phase-parent\",\n  \"build\": \"npm run prepare-build && tsc --build && npm run record-build\",\n  \"record-build\": \"node lib/dist-freshness.cjs record-build --package system-spec-kit/runtime/cli --entry default && node lib/dist-freshness.cjs record-build --package system-spec-kit/runtime/cli --entry is-phase-parent\",\n  \"rebuild\": \"npm run clean && npm run build\",\n  \"typecheck\": \"tsc --noEmit --composite false -p tsconfig.json\",\n  \"lint\": \"tsc --noEmit\",\n  \"pretest\": \"npm run build\",\n  \"test\": \"vitest run --config ../../vitest.config.ts --project cli && npm run test:legacy && npm run test:validation\",\n  \"test:task-enrichment\": \"vitest run tests/task-enrichment.vitest.ts --config ../vitest.config.ts --root .\",\n  \"test:legacy\": \"npm run build && node tests/test-scripts-modules.js && node tests/test-extractors-loaders.js && node tests/test-phase-validation.js && node tests/test-phase-system.js\",\n  \"test:validation\": \"node tests/test-validation-system.cjs && bash tests/test-validation.sh && bash tests/test-validation-extended.sh && bash tests/check-ac-closure.sh && bash tests/check-ac-coverage.sh && bash tests/check-graph-metadata-child-drift.sh && bash tests/check-graph-metadata-shape-last-active-child.sh && bash tests/test-phase-system.sh\",\n  \"check:ast\": \"npx tsx evals/check-no-mcp-lib-imports-ast.ts && npx tsx evals/check-handler-cycles-ast.ts\",\n  \"check\": \"npm run lint && npx tsx evals/check-no-mcp-lib-imports.ts && bash check-api-boundary.sh && npx tsx evals/check-architecture-boundaries.ts && npx tsx evals/check-allowlist-expiry.ts && npx tsx evals/check-source-dist-alignment.ts && npx tsx evals/check-no-mcp-lib-imports-ast.ts && npx tsx evals/check-handler-cycles-ast.ts\"\n}\n"}}],"_meta":{"cognition.ai/cwd":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Code-Environment-Public/fcd93cd7-b3f2-45e6-b976-87fabe792df3/scratchpad/speed-loop/w4fbf614733/tree","terminal_exit":{"terminal_id":"50b239","exit_code":0,"signal":null},"cognition.ai/inferenceToolName":"exec"}}
